+# Antigravity host reference
+
+Read only when selecting an Antigravity destination or explaining invocation.
+Verified against the [official skills documentation](https://antigravity.google/docs/skills)
+on 2026-10-12. Host versions can change; use the active interface's documented root.
+
+## Project scope
+
+Use `<workspace>/.agents/skills/<skill_name>/SKILL.md`. The legacy
+`.agent/skills` root is supported for compatibility but is not needed when the
+shared `.agents/skills` source already exists. Keep relative references and helper
+scripts inside the skill so the same files serve all requested hosts.
+
+Both `name` and `description` are present in this package; Antigravity requires
+`description` and accepts the common YAML-frontmatter + Markdown structure.
+Do not add a second manifest or infer support for another host's tool grants.
+
+## Personal scope
+
+| Interface | Root |
+|---|---|
+| Antigravity 2.0 / IDE | `~/.gemini/config/skills/` |
+| Antigravity CLI | `~/.gemini/antigravity-cli/skills/` |
+| Legacy IDE compatibility | `~/.gemini/antigravity/skills/` |
+
+Identify the active interface before choosing a personal destination. A generic
+personal `~/.agents/skills` install is not an Antigravity discovery claim.
+
+## Invocation and evidence
+
+Use a natural-language request naming `book-to-skill` and the source document.
+Antigravity 2.0/CLI documents `/<skill-name>` invocation; the IDE can use the
+named natural-language request and inspect enabled skills under Customizations.
+
+After writing files, verify the selected root, frontmatter, links, and helper
+execution. These checks prove filesystem readiness. Report actual app discovery
+only after observing it in the active host. This project uses the physical
+`.agents/skills` directory, so no assumption about Antigravity symlink support
+is required.
